// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// T27 OS pty_server: the long-lived process that owns one pseudo-terminal per pane, so an agent CLI
// (Claude Code, Codex, a shell) keeps running when the window closes or crashes (the herdr.dev model).
// It spawns the pane's command in the pane's cwd, keeps a 64 KiB scrollback ring per pane, serves the
// frames of pty_proto.t27 on ~/.t27os/pty.sock, and writes one record per pane under ~/.t27os/sessions
// (session_store.t27) on every change. When the server dies, its masters close, the panes get SIGHUP, and
// the next start reads the records and brings every pane back by the agents.t27 RESUME_* rules.
//
// One binary, three modes, picked by the environment so no argv parsing is needed:
//   (none)             serve
//   T27OS_HOOK=1       a Claude Code hook: read the payload on stdin, forward it as OP_HOOK to pane
//                      T27OS_PANE, exit. The server writes ~/.t27os/hooks.json so claude panes run it.
//   T27OS_CTL=<verb>   a tiny client for scripts and the live test: list, spawn, kill, read, write (keys)
//                      (T27OS_AGENT, T27OS_CWD, T27OS_MODEL, T27OS_PANE, T27OS_KEYS carry the arguments).
//                      An editor pane (T27 OS opens inside, 2026-10-20) is spawn with T27OS_AGENT=9 (the
//                      shell cell) and T27OS_MODEL=vim|nvim|hx|micro|nano: the pane runs that editor on
//                      T27OS_CWD, a folder or a file, instead of bash (pty_logic launch_command).
//   T27OS_INSTALL=1    write ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ai.t27.os-server.plist for this binary: it starts
//                      the server at login, so panes come back (by session id, model kept) after a reboot.
//
// Keys (gHashTag/t27#11241): the server holds up to MAX_KEYS numbered keys for each provider, in memory only,
// sent by the window with OP_SETKEY (the key number rides in the high nibble of the pane byte). Every agent
// pane picks its key by rotation at each start; the pane record keeps the key NUMBER, never the key. The
// claude cell's screen is read for an error row (pty_logic screen_text, keys.t27 error_row and classify_line):
// the failed key rests, the pane is respawned (resumed) on the next key or profile, or stays with a line in its
// scrollback. A restored pane waits for a key (or 20 s) before it starts. T27OS_CTL=list prints "key N" for
// each pane.
// The server does not depend on the window for its keys: it reads the Keychain itself, through the same
// /usr/bin/security reader the window uses (keys_host kc_get_n, no SecItem call, no dialog), once at its start
// before it restores panes and again at a spawn that finds no key for its agent when the last read is older than
// a minute (pty_logic keys_reload_due, load_mask_agent). A read puts each key in the table by the code path of
// OP_SETKEY (put_key), so a pane spawned while the window is closed, minimized or never connected is logged in,
// a restarted server is not keyless, and a key added from a terminal is picked up. A window's OP_SETKEY still
// works and overrides or adds.
//
// Every decision is a fn with a test that runs; the host loop only moves bytes through pty_sys.t27.
//
// Refs gHashTag/t27#10782.
module T27osPtyServer;

